@page "/"
@using BookHeaven.Web.Components
<PageTitle>Home | BookHeaven</PageTitle>

<section class="text-center mb-10 md:mb-20 max-w-[700px] mx-auto">
	<p class="font-bold text-4xl md:text-6xl mb-10">
		Take <span class="text-(--color-primary)">control</span><br/>of your digital library
	</p>
	<p class="text-lg md:text-2xl text-balance break-keep mb-10">
		BookHeaven is a tiny <span class="text-(--color-primary)">self-hosted</span> ecosystem that helps you manage and read your e-books in a very <span class="text-(--color-primary)">convenient</span> way.
	</p>
	<p class="italic text-balance mb-10 md:mb-20">Check out what each part of the ecosystem can do for you down below,<br class="hidden sm:inline"/> and press this button to make your life easier.</p>
	<a class="mx-auto text-2xl bg-(--color-primary) px-5 py-2 rounded-lg font-bold uppercase hover:bg-(--color-primary)/70 transition-colors" href="https://github.com/BookHeaven/BookHeaven.Server">Get Started</a>
</section>
<hr class="my-10 md:my-20 text-neutral-700"/>
<section class="flex flex-col">
	<h1 class="text-nowrap text-2xl md:text-4xl font-bold">BookHeaven <span class="text-(--color-primary)">Server</span></h1>
	<div class="flex items-center gap-2 mt-3">
		<Pill Text="web" />
		<Pill Text="docker" />
	</div>
	<p class="my-5 ms-2 text-slate-300">
		Upload your e-books and organize them to your liking into authors, series and tags. You can also upload fonts so your devices can download and use them.<br/>
		It's really easy to set up and use, and you can run it on any device that supports Docker.<br/>
	</p>
	<img src="img/server-img.png" class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-(--color-primary) glow mt-10 mx-2 md:mx-5" alt="" />
</section>
<hr class="my-10 md:my-20 text-neutral-700"/>
<section class="flex flex-col">
	<h1 class="text-nowrap text-2xl md:text-4xl font-bold">BookHeaven <span class="text-(--color-primary)">Reader</span></h1>
	<div class="flex items-center gap-2 mt-3">
		<Pill Text="android"/>
		<Pill Text="e-reader"/>
		<Pill Text="e-ink"/>
		<Pill Text="launcher"/>
	</div>
	<p class="my-5 ms-2 text-slate-300">
		If you have an android e-reader, you are in luck. With this app you'll be able to connect to your server and easily download and read all of your books.<br/>
		But not only that, it will also track your progress and reading time for each book, which you can manually sync to your server at any time.<br/>
		No connection required at all for regular use, so you can save your precious battery life.
	</p>
	<div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-1 bg-black overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border-2 border-(--color-primary) glow px-2 md:px-5 pt-2 md:pt-5 mt-10 mx-2 md:mx-5">
		<img src="img/reader-img.png" class="grayscale" alt=""/>
		<img src="img/reader-book.png" class="grayscale" alt=""/>
		<img src="img/reader-apps.png" class="grayscale" alt=""/>
	</div>
</section>